# 6. UNIFIED RULES INTELLIGENCE ENGINE

This is the foundation of the complete platform.

Every module must use the same shared rules database and evidence system.

## Main responsibilities

- Read official PDFs and notifications.
- Extract document text.
- Extract structured rules and conditions.
- Preserve page and clause references.
- Store document versions.
- Track effective dates.
- Identify possible conflicts.
- Connect rules to procedures and requirements.
- Maintain verification status.
- Provide evidence to the other modules.

## Document ingestion workflow

1. Administrator uploads an official PDF.
2. System checks whether the PDF contains selectable text.
3. If selectable text exists, extract it page by page.
4. If it is scanned, use OCR when supported.
5. Store the original document securely.
6. Store extracted page text.
7. Record extraction confidence.
8. Pass the extracted text for structured rule extraction.
9. Save extracted rules as drafts.
10. Send uncertain results for human review.

## Structured rule format

Every extracted rule should contain:

- Rule ID
- Document ID
- Scheme ID, if applicable
- Rule type
- Condition in simple language
- Machine-readable field
- Operator
- Value
- Applicable user group
- Source document
- Page number
- Clause reference
- Extraction confidence
- Verification status
- Valid-from date
- Valid-to date

Example:

Field: family_income  
Operator: less_than_or_equal_to  
Value: 250000  
Rule type: eligibility condition  
Status: draft

This is an illustrative example, not a real government eligibility rule.

## Rule status

- Draft
- Under review
- Active
- Superseded
- Rejected

Only approved and active rules can power official-facing guidance.

## Important technical principle

The AI extracts and explains rules.

Ordinary deterministic application code evaluates structured eligibility conditions.

Do not use an AI model as the final eligibility calculator.

